# LOG_084: Engineer Town Market Day - Potato Value Chain

**Date:** 2026-08-12
**Location:** Engineer Town, Nyandarua County, KE
**Classification:** Field Observation → Market Node → Stage II
**Status:** Canonical
**Tags:** #Fieldwork #EngineerTown #Market #Potato #FolkInfrastructure #9PointDiagnostic #Gikuyu

## 1. Institutions Identified
AFA, AGRA, NPCK, KENFA, GTZ, KALRO, ICP, County Government, Community Groups

## 2. Actors in the Chain
Farmers → Brokers/Local Traders → Processors(Midland Ltd) → Wholesalers → Retailers/Eateries/Supermarkets → Households

## 3. Local Infrastructure Signals
**Language:** Gikuyu dominant. Market lingo: Dusura, Ndoo/Bucket, Irebe
**Packaging:** Mukurino, Kata/Kamba, Dusura bags. No 50kg standard enforced.
**Varieties:** Shangi, Tigoni dominate
**Grading:** No standardized system. Top tier only for Midland Ltd.

## 4. Bottlenecks Observed
Distance/time to market, Manhandling damage, Poor storage, 
Weights/measures discrepancies, Repackaging losses, Wastage

## 5. Gates Hit Hardest
Gate 3: Payments → No metric standard = trust issue
Gate 5: Distribution → Distance, time, manhandling
Gate 7: Intelligence → Prices static, supply/demand only
Gate 2: Trust → Each level has own weighing scale

## 6. Folk Infrastructure Present
Market lingo, bag types as risk hedges, broker pecking order

